-- title:
--   Fpqc-local lifting through the fine Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation
-- statement:
--   The setting is the one in which the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of a fine quaternionic moduli scheme is formulated, and the hypotheses come in the following groups.
--
--   **Arithmetic of the base.** Two distinct primes $r \neq \bar r$ and a nonzero level $N$ with $r \nmid N$ and $\bar r \nmid N$. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring, with an irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete (`IsAdicComplete (Ideal.span {π}) 𝒪`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$, so that $\mathcal O$ is absolutely unramified with residue field $\mathbb F_r$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field realised as the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A further characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element of $Onr$ a root modulo $\pi$ of a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$; thus $Onr$ plays the role of the completion of the maximal unramified extension with its Frobenius lift. Finally a homomorphism $vdet : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet\,g = n$ exactly when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$; that is, $vdet$ is the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant.
--
--   **The indefinite algebra and its coarse moduli scheme.** Rationals $a, b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra precisely when $v$ lies over $r$ or over $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (an order not properly contained in any order). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with $f : \mathcal X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O$ and an assignment $pt$ sending a fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-multiplication and level-$N$ structure over an $\mathcal O$-algebra $S$ to an $S$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O$, such that `IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳 f pt` holds: $pt$ is invariant under isomorphism of fake elliptic curves, compatible with pullback along ring maps, bijective on geometric points over algebraically closed fields (surjective, and injective up to isomorphism), and universal among such isomorphism-invariant, pullback-compatible assignments.
--
--   **The fine moduli scheme with full level $n$ and its twisting action.** An integer $n \geq 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n, N) = 1$; a scheme $M$ with $f_M : M \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathcal O$ and an assignment $ptF$ on fake elliptic curves equipped with a full level-$n$ structure, satisfying `IsFineModuli Λ N n M fM ptF`: isomorphism-invariance, compatibility with pullback, and bijectivity of $ptF$ on $S$-points for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $S$ (not merely on geometric points). A group $G$, a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ and a map $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ with `IsLevelTwistAction`: each $\rho(g)$ is a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, twisting a full level structure by $\chi(g)$ is realised on moduli points by composition with $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n\Lambda$ in the sense of the four labelling clauses of that structure.
--
--   **Compatibilities.** A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, invariant under the $G$-action, with $ptF(u)$ followed by $p$ equal to $pt(u_1)$ for every full-level object $u$ with underlying fake elliptic curve $u_1$.
--
--   **The Hecke tower away from $r$ and $\bar r$.** For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and an assignment $ptT_\ell$ on fake elliptic curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup, satisfying `IsCoarseModuliT` (the analogue of the coarse moduli conditions for that problem); two degeneracy morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, where $d_0$ forgets the extra level and $d_1$ is compatible with passing to a quotient along a level-$\ell$ isogeny in the sense of `FakeEllipticCurve.IsLevelIsogeny`.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner morphisms.** Endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ realising on moduli points the relation `FakeEllipticCurve.IsAtkinLehnerQuotient` at $r$ and at $\bar r$ respectively.
--
--   **The definite frame.** Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`, i.e. $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1] \otimes \mathbb Q_v$ a division algebra exactly at the place above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$; a finite-adelic unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ (`meetOrder R₁ n₁`) is an Eichler order of level $N r$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ characterised by `hΓt` as [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), namely the units whose image at every height-one prime $w \neq v$ lies in the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R_1$ at $w$. Families $s_\ell$ of global units and $sf_\ell$ of finite-adelic units indexed by the primes $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ subject to `hs` (four clauses): $sf_\ell$ localises to $s_\ell \otimes 1$ at every prime not containing $r$, localises to $1$ at primes containing $r$, the product of the adelic diagonal image of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; and subgroups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$. A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$. A homomorphism $\theta_t : \Gamma_t \to G$.
--
--   **The uniformisation family.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map
--   $$\Theta_f : \bigl(\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O\text{-alg}}(Onr, B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}_{\pi}(B)\bigr) \times G \longrightarrow \{\varphi : \operatorname{Spec} B \to M \ \text{over} \ \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O\},$$
--   where the middle factor is the value at $B$ of the functor `Omega K₀ π` (a $B$-submodule $\mathrm{line}(L)$ of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} L$ for every full lattice $L \subset K_0^2$, with invertible quotient, monotone in $L$, equivariant for scalar homotheties and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$), and the target is the value at $B$ of `Scheme.nilpPoints fM`. It is subject to: `hnat`, naturality in $B$ along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps; `hG`, that composing with $\rho(h)$ sends $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ to $\Theta_f(x, g)$; `hinv`, that if $x'$ is obtained from $x$ by the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ — that is, the $Onr$-component of $x'$ is the $Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0\gamma)}$-twist of that of $x$, and the Deligne datum of $x'$ is the pullback of that of $x$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ — then $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma) g) = \Theta_f(x, g)$; `het`, formal étaleness: for every surjection $p : B \to B_0$ of $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent whose kernel has square zero, and every $x_0$ over $B_0$ and $y$ over $B$ with $p_*y = \Theta_f(x_0)$, there is a unique $x$ over $B$ lifting $x_0$ with $\Theta_f(x) = y$; and `hgeom`, the description over algebraically closed fields $k$ with $\pi$ nilpotent: for each $\psi : Onr \to k$ every $k$-point of $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ is of the form $\Theta_f((\psi, P), g)$, and $\Theta_f((\psi, P), g) = \Theta_f((\psi', P'), g')$ holds if and only if there is $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ with $g' = \theta_t(\gamma) g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and with $\psi'(y) = (\psi \circ Fr^{-vdet(\iota_0\gamma)})(y)$ for every $y \in Onr$ which is fixed by $Fr^{vdet(\iota_0 z)}$ for all scalar $z \in \Gamma_t$ with $\theta_t(z) = 1$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and every point $y : \operatorname{Spec} B \to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, there exist a natural number $k$ and a family of commutative rings $B'_i$, $i \in \{0, \dots, k-1\}$, each carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a $B$-algebra structure compatible in the tower $\mathcal O \to B \to B'_i$, such that:
--
--   1. each $B'_i$ is flat as a $B$-module;
--
--   2. the family is jointly surjective on spectra: every prime ideal of $B$ is the contraction of some prime ideal of some $B'_i$;
--
--   3. the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent in each $B'_i$;
--
--   4. there are points $x'_i$ of $\bigl(\operatorname{Hom}_{\mathcal O\text{-alg}}(Onr, -) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}_{\pi}(-)\bigr) \times G$ over $B'_i$ with $\Theta_f(x'_i) = y|_{B'_i}$, the restriction being the image of $y$ under the map induced by the structure morphism $B \to B'_i$.
--
--   No finiteness of $B'_i$ over $B$, and no étaleness, is asserted: the covering is flat and jointly surjective, hence $\prod_i B'_i$ is faithfully flat over $B$.
--
--   This is the fpqc-local form of the surjectivity of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation map $\Theta_f$ on the nilpotent-points functor of the fine quaternionic moduli scheme $M$: an arbitrary point of $M$ over a base in which $\pi$ is nilpotent becomes a point of the uniformising functor after a finite flat covering of the base. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.existsUnique_factor_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.existsUnique_factor_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine), where the local lifts are glued by descent to produce the factorisation of morphisms through the uniformisation.
